From 6a5fcbc14290b6fb67e90be7cd39ffb2d5b2f4b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Belke <andreas.belke@governikus.de>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 14:35:54 +0200
Subject: a11y: make checkable buttons toggle on activation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a screen reader (Narrator, NVDA, VoiceOver, TalkBack) activates a
QQuickAbstractButton-derived control, the control should behave as if
the user had released a mouse, touch, or key on it: for a checkable
button that means the check state must flip and toggled() must be
emitted, in addition to clicked().
Applications should not need to wire Accessible.onPressAction or
Accessible.onToggleAction handlers to get consistent toggling
across platforms - that is the default behaviour pointer and
keyboard activation already provide, and a11y activation should
match.

The bug has two parts

* NVDA, TalkBack, iOS VoiceOver land on pressAction(), which
  QAccessibleQuickItem::doAction() dispatches to the Qt slot
  accessiblePressAction() on the item. Before this patch that slot
  called trigger() only, which emits clicked() but leaves the check
  state alone.
* MacOS VoiceOver, Narrator creates a toggleAction().
  No accessibleToggleAction() slot existed on QQuickAbstractButton, so
  the call fell through to the generic role fallback in
  QAccessibleQuickItem::doAction() that sets the "checked" property via
  QObject::setProperty(). Neither toggled() or clicked() was emitted.
  Also toggling disabled controls was possible.

Route the a11y press default slot through QQuickAbstractButton::click(),
the same way QAccessibleButton::doAction() in qtbase. That emits the
same signals as a real touch, mouse, or keyboard release and respects
the disabled state. Do the same for toggle action. Declare
accessibleToggleAction() as a public slot so
QAccessibleQuickItem::doAction() finds it via
QMetaObject::invokeMethod() for the "Toggle" action name, before the
role fallback runs.

This follows the qtbase (widgets) fix
5317ff74fd2ff31e4bfb8e7e6c4a6e06a16fffc8, which argued that toggleAction
only produces toggled(), but users may be more discerning and listen
only to clicked() to react to *user* events, not every toggle.

When the user has wired Accessible.onPressAction or
Accessible.onToggleAction explicitly,
QQuickAccessibleAttached::doAction() continues to accept the action
before any default slot runs, so this change is source- and
behaviour-compatible with existing code that opts in to custom handling.

Fixes: QTBUG-144350
Pick-to: 6.11
